00:00:36.669 --> 00:00:37.971 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:37.971 --> 00:00:41.775 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Quit wriggling around.
I'm trying to count your ribs!

00:00:41.775 --> 00:00:45.645 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:45.645 --> 00:00:47.147 size:81% position:41% line:92%
[ Laughter continues ]

00:00:47.147 --> 00:00:50.750
The alphabetizing thing is not
true -- at least, in my case

00:00:50.750 --> 00:00:52.285 align:start size:94% position:6%
People think
I'm weirder than I am,

00:00:52.285 --> 00:00:53.887 line:92%
and it's hard for me, you know

00:00:53.887 --> 00:00:54.421 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:54.421 --> 00:00:57.090 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, they ask questions, like
"Brian with your OCD,

00:00:57.090 --> 00:01:00.260 align:start size:94% position:6%
do you have to alphabetize
your books at home?"

00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:02.395 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I'm, like, "Uh, no."
[ Laughter ]

00:01:02.395 --> 00:01:06.933 align:start size:94% position:6%
"I organize my books by
when I got them chronologicall

00:01:06.933 --> 00:01:08.368 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
on the top shelf."

00:01:08.368 --> 00:01:09.335 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:09.335 --> 00:01:11.304 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't have to alphabetiz
my books.

00:01:11.304 --> 00:01:12.505 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I'm not a kook.

00:01:12.505 --> 00:01:14.841 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:14.841 --> 00:01:18.545
And the bottom shelf is fo
the books I finished reading

00:01:18.545 --> 00:01:20.246 line:92%
organized chronologically.

00:01:20.246 --> 00:01:20.780 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:23.850 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't have to
alphabetize them. Mnh.

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:25.285 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:25.285 --> 00:01:27.554 size:75% position:38% line:92%
And the middle shelf

00:01:27.554 --> 00:01:30.390 align:start size:94% position:6%
is for the books
I'm in the process of reading.

00:01:30.390 --> 00:01:31.991 align:start size:94% position:6%
Those are organized
chronologically.

00:01:31.991 --> 00:01:33.693 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
When I start reading a book,

00:01:33.693 --> 00:01:36.963 align:start size:94% position:6%
I just move it from the
top shelf to the middle shelf,

00:01:36.963 --> 00:01:38.731 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I know exactly what
you're wondering --

00:01:38.731 --> 00:01:41.801 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Well, wouldn't reading
the title of the book coun

00:01:41.801 --> 00:01:45.738
technically as being in th
process of reading the book?

00:01:45.738 --> 00:01:46.873 line:92%
Then how would you distinguish

00:01:46.873 --> 00:01:49.609 size:81% position:41%
between the top shelf
and the middle shelf?"

00:01:49.609 --> 00:01:51.511 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:51.511 --> 00:01:53.980 size:88% position:44% line:92%
Well, the way I do it --

00:01:53.980 --> 00:01:56.716 align:start size:94% position:6%
I make myself read
all of page one

00:01:56.716 --> 00:01:59.185 line:92%
before I allow a shelf change.

00:01:59.185 --> 00:02:01.121 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:01.121 --> 00:02:04.124 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't count the introduction
or the forward

00:02:04.124 --> 00:02:04.891 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
or the book jacket.

00:02:04.891 --> 00:02:07.627 align:start size:94% position:6%
I do read all of that
word for word,

00:02:07.627 --> 00:02:10.563 align:start size:94% position:6%
but then I make myself rea
all of page one,

00:02:10.563 --> 00:02:11.998 line:92%
all the way to the bottom...

00:02:11.998 --> 00:02:13.900 align:start size:94% position:6%
unless it ends
in the middle of a sentence --

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:15.969 align:start size:94% position:6%
I make myself turn the page.
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:15.969 --> 00:02:18.771 align:start size:94% position:6%
I finish the sentence
to complete the thought.

00:02:18.771 --> 00:02:19.506 size:78% position:39% line:92%
I turn the page back.

00:02:19.506 --> 00:02:21.441
I write down what date that book
was started

00:02:21.441 --> 00:02:22.842 align:start size:94% position:6%
and move that
to the middle shelf

00:02:22.842 --> 00:02:23.743 size:81% position:41% line:92%
furthest on the right.

00:02:23.743 --> 00:02:25.545 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't have to alphabetiz
my books.

00:02:25.545 --> 00:02:27.147 size:84% position:42% line:92%
I'm not out of my mind!

00:02:27.147 --> 00:02:29.215 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:29.215 --> 00:02:33.019 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:33.019 --> 00:02:35.255 size:81% position:41% line:92%
[ Applause continues ]

00:02:35.255 --> 00:02:39.492
You know, when I first suspected
that I might have OCD,

00:02:39.492 --> 00:02:40.326 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I Googled it.

00:02:40.326 --> 00:02:41.794 align:start size:94% position:6%
And there are
different symptoms,

00:02:41.794 --> 00:02:43.396 align:start size:94% position:6%
and some I have,
and some I don't.

00:02:43.396 --> 00:02:47.233
And the ones I have, some I have
more strongly than others.

00:02:47.233 --> 00:02:50.370 size:75% position:38%
So I decided to make
a color-coded graph.

00:02:50.370 --> 00:02:52.005 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:52.005 --> 00:02:53.673 line:92%
I wish I was making this up.

00:02:53.673 --> 00:02:54.607 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:54.607 --> 00:02:56.242 align:start size:94% position:6%
I listed the symptoms,
and I said,

00:02:56.242 --> 00:02:58.411 align:start size:94% position:6%
